{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{artist: Robert Burns (1788)}
{key: G}
{tempo: 72}
{strum: D.DU.UDU}

Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be forgot,
And [G]never brought to [C]mind?
Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be forgot,
And [Em]auld [C]lang [D]syne[G]?

{start_of_chorus}
For [G]auld lang [D]syne, my dear,
For [G]auld lang [C]syne,
We'll [G]take a cup o' [D]kindness yet,
For [Em]auld [C]lang [D]syne[G].
{end_of_chorus}
